md+=['','These are different source populations. They overlap and include repeated orders, actions, scheduled observations and pair-feature rows. Do not sum them as independent trades or join by row position. P08/P09 cohort counts differ on October 3 and 18; no cross-study identity was assumed.','', '## Timing, feedback and contrary evidence','','| Date | Changes without fresh classified volume / all ratio changes | Eligible at +25ms / rest episodes | Recognition median seconds | After-recognition 60s mean ticks (N; + / − / flat) |','|---|---|---|---:|---|']
for d in days:
 v=metric(d,'after_recognition_oriented_60s_ticks');md += [f"| {d} | {C[d]['flow_age_only_changes']:,}/{C[d]['flow_ratio_changes']:,} | {C[d]['rest_eligible_25ms']:,}/{C[d]['rest_events']:,} | {metric(d,'recognition_elapsed_s')['median']:.3f} | {v['mean']:.3f} ({v['n']}; {v['positive']}/{v['negative']}/{v['flat']}) |"]
md += ['', 'Flow changes without fresh classified volume arise as classified volume leaves the rolling window; unknown-side events remain a separate category. No original completed-second clock precedes its second end; the final second of each session lacks a completion clock and remains unavailable. Completion can be delayed substantially in quiet markets.','','The 60-second response table is an outcome diagnostic, not a warning lead, entry fill, net edge, or proposed exit time. Observations are overlapping, costs are excluded, and all four dates already informed discovery. Recognition-direction median response at 60 seconds is zero on every date. Flow/book agreement is not uniformly better than disagreement.','','Full-depth sign is positive in 3,068 of 3,215 family rows, while touch depth can disagree. Full depth and touch are not interchangeable. Categorical `+`, `-`, `0`, `NA` were parsed explicitly; an event-order sentinel of -1 was excluded from observed-order comparisons and retained as censored. These checks changed the draft analysis before delivery.','','Additional saved-cell feedback checks in price_feedback_cells.json compare prior 20-second price direction with current five-second flow and full-depth versus touch signs, followed by future price response. They preserve reverse-order and neutral/missing cases. They do not identify causal price impact, since family/cohort selection is retrospective and a complete intervening action-path causal analysis has not been performed.','','## Case evidence and coverage','','analysis_cases.json retains deterministic examples per date and state, including opposed, missing, adverse fate, expired and surviving orders. Each case names its sheet, actual Excel row, source ID, zero-based source row and complete cell values. It is an illustration index, not a filtered population used for metrics. cell_metrics.csv and Priority metrics contain all computed distributions; Priority counts retains population and clock-check counts.','','The prior master coverage remains: 143,270 saved trades and 141 original layer fields via the existing companion layer workbooks. Existing companion research is not re-exported or silently replaced. Original corrected sources S00092/S00096/S00101/S00105 remain intact. The archived 193k dipole-stage table is context only, not admitted as newly verified event data. The claimed ~0.5-second warning remains unverified. The exact identities of the earlier “two workflows” remain unresolved; this report makes no new claim about their results.','','## First paper rules','','PAPER_STRATEGIES.md and PAPER_STRATEGIES.json freeze R1 fresh-flow/touch agreement with a strictly later quote confirmation, and R2 observed surviving-order absorption with later quote confirmation. Paper rules v1 contains the complete specification in the main Excel workbook. Both are prospective hypotheses; the selected studies do not test these composite rules as a strategy.','','Shared provisional limits: one virtual standard NG contract total, four-tick stop trigger, twelve-tick session loss limit, 120-second holding cap, thirty-second cooldown and twenty entries per configured session. No averaging or automatic reversal. Marketable IOC fills require a subsequent executable quote and measured arrival; passive survival and scheduled offsets never stand in for our fills. Gross, fees, net and adverse-slippage stress are separate. Unknown fees produce unavailable net PnL.','','PAPER_READINESS.md lists the remaining execution-adapter configuration and acceptance cases. No adapter was connected and no trades were submitted. The workbook/rules are ready for review and adapter implementation; execution readiness is conditional on that configuration and its checks.','','## Deferred reconciliation','','The previously running bulk jobs finished without duplicate launches. Workflow retained 18,168,382 rows; the Oct 2 workflow export finished 4,340,150 rows in 255 books. Remaining-source processing and source-sample reconciliation reached durable checkpoints. These bulk outputs are not claimed to be fully cell-verified or included in this priority delivery. Other workflow dates and exhaustive publication remain deferred for the next session.','']
